Now let's talk a little about Russian culture.

00:04:57.860 --> 00:05:01.500
The bear, medved, is very, very special in Russia.

00:05:02.060 --> 00:05:05.040
It has been the symbol of the country for hundreds of years.

00:05:05.040 --> 00:05:12.680
Russians see the bear as strong and powerful, but also a bit clumsy and very protective of its family.

00:05:13.420 --> 00:05:18.760
In old Russian fairy tales, the bear is almost always called by a friendly name,

00:05:19.400 --> 00:05:24.580
Michail Potapic, which is like calling him Michael the Bear.

00:05:25.020 --> 00:05:31.160
It makes him feel like a big, lovable uncle, rather than a scary wild animal.

00:05:31.160 --> 00:05:37.880
Russian children grow up surrounded by teddy bears, bear cartoons, and hundreds of bear stories.

00:05:38.320 --> 00:05:43.820
Even today, many Russian kids sleep with a plush medved in their arms.

