00:06:57.600 --> 00:07:00.500
That makes it so much easier to remember forever.

00:07:01.520 --> 00:07:02.480
Want to hear the secret?

00:07:03.400 --> 00:07:08.480
Long, long ago, people in the forest were afraid to say the real ancient name of the bear.

00:07:09.060 --> 00:07:15.460
They believed that if you spoke its true name, the big bear might hear you and come to your house.

00:07:15.460 --> 00:07:19.680
So instead of saying the dangerous word, they created a polite nickname.

00:07:20.280 --> 00:07:24.320
The one who knows honey, or honey eta.

00:07:25.460 --> 00:07:27.580
That's exactly where medved comes from.

00:07:28.200 --> 00:07:31.740
Med, honey, plus ved, knows.

00:07:32.540 --> 00:07:37.860
It's a beautiful example of how Russian language reflects culture and old beliefs.

00:07:38.540 --> 00:07:41.920
English kept a different ancient route for bear,

00:07:41.920 --> 00:07:47.200
